51. Healthy BMI-[POSITIVE]->Norm BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.177605690016523, 'original_motivation': "'Healthy BMI' does not cause 'Norm BMI' because neither variable is defined, and there is no known direct causal link between them. Without definitions, measurement, or mechanisms, no causal relationship can be established in either direction.", 'session_id': '846d2a58-f8dc-4b58-9c66-3ce0744ebd44', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5850018935073062, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09361693537991114, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation is somewhat circular, as \\"maintaining a healthy BMI\\" and \\"having a normal BMI\\" are conceptually very similar, if not the same. The explanation does not clearly distinguish between cause and effect because maintaining a healthy BMI essentially means keeping BMI in the normal range. Therefore, saying that maintaining a healthy BMI causes BMI to become normal is tautological and does not provide a meaningful causal mechanism beyond restating the definitions. However, the mention of \\"healthy lifestyle choices\\" adjusting body composition does add a partial causal pathway, but it is not directly between the source and target variables as named.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6854170263000603, 'motivation': "Maintaining a healthy BMI directly causes an individual's BMI to become more 'normal' over time, as healthy lifestyle choices actively adjust body composition toward the norm. Therefore, adopting habits that promote a healthy BMI will directly move a person's BMI into the normal range.", 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "Maintaining a healthy BMI directly causes an individual's BMI to become more 'normal' over time, as healthy lifestyle choices actively adjust body composition toward the norm. Therefore, adopting habits that promote a healthy BMI will directly move a person's BMI into the normal range.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.016725045223000532, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7475336595445344, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.000327922502234252, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3059688470741934}

