63. Socio-cultural Ideal BMI-[POSITIVE]->Individual Ideal BMI
   Properties: {'session_id': '846d2a58-f8dc-4b58-9c66-3ce0744ebd44', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4121824741406874, 'citations': ['https://med.stanford.edu/news/insights/2024/11/bmi-body-mass-index-alternatives-science.html', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK535456/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4890841/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_mass_index', 'https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/index.html'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07885414646915817, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation describes a process where individual preferences for BMI shape and eventually determine the socio-cultural ideal BMI through aggregation. This implies a causal direction from Individual Ideal BMI to Socio-cultural Ideal BMI, not the other way around. However, the relationship being evaluated is from Socio-cultural Ideal BMI (source) to Individual Ideal BMI (target), so the explanation does not support the claimed causal direction. Therefore, the reasoning is internally inconsistent for the specified direction of causality.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7785101036007546, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7372990313831389, 'motivation': 'Socio-cultural Ideal BMI and Individual Ideal BMI exhibit a positive relationship because individuals who personally prefer a higher or lower BMI tend to seek out and participate in social groups or media environments that reflect and reinforce their own ideals. As a result, the collective Socio-cultural Ideal BMI within these environments gradually aligns with the pre-existing Individual Ideal BMI of their members. This aggregation of similar personal preferences drives the observed correlation, as shifts in Individual Ideal BMI precede and shape broader socio-cultural standards.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 