   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.078841735462127, 'original_motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) causes Body Mass Index (BMI) to change in an inverse causal relationship. Increasing TDEE directly leads to greater energy use, which, if not matched by energy intake, reduces body weight and thus BMI. Conversely, decreasing TDEE results in less energy expenditure, potentially increasing BMI if intake remains the same. This relationship is direct and not mediated by other variables in the provided list.', 'session_id': '846d2a58-f8dc-4b58-9c66-3ce0744ebd44', 'judge_perplexity': 1.449327824319549, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0797494335420411, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that higher energy expenditure (TDEE) causes higher BMI because burning more calories leads to more fat storage. This is internally inconsistent: burning more calories should, all else equal, reduce energy available for storage, not increase it. The reasoning confuses the direction of causality between energy expenditure and fat accumulation. Therefore, the causal reasoning is flawed.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.695640231054888, 'motivation': 'A higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) directly causes an increase in Body Mass Index (BMI) because burning more calories makes the body store extra energy as fat. Therefore, individuals who expend more energy throughout the day will have higher BMI values.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'A higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) directly causes an increase in Body Mass Index (BMI) because burning more calories makes the body store extra energy as fat. Therefore, individuals who expend more energy throughout the day will have higher BMI values.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.11985414309700781, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7712256840796597, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.0010662849696328573, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2823994219931073}

