   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.13389580527449, 'original_motivation': 'Body Mass Index (BMI) causes Basal Metabolic Rate to change in a direct causal relationship. As BMI increases—reflecting greater body mass—Basal Metabolic Rate typically increases because a larger body requires more energy to maintain basic physiological functions. Conversely, a decrease in BMI leads to a lower Basal Metabolic Rate. This causal effect is due to the direct link between total body mass and metabolic energy expenditure.', 'session_id': '846d2a58-f8dc-4b58-9c66-3ce0744ebd44', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5527841387598669, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08907937489141966, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that a higher BMI causes the body to lower its basal metabolic rate as a means of conserving energy and preventing further weight gain. Internally, this logic is flawed, as it assumes the body deliberately reduces energy expenditure when body mass increases, without providing a plausible physiological mechanism. Typically, greater body mass would require more energy to maintain, so the reasoning here does not logically support a negative relationship between BMI and basal metabolic rate.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7146526828040197, 'motivation': 'A higher Body Mass Index (BMI) indicates greater body mass, which the body interprets as a signal to conserve energy. As a result, the basal metabolic rate decreases in order to prevent further weight gain, so there is a negative relationship between BMI and basal metabolic rate.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'A higher Body Mass Index (BMI) indicates greater body mass, which the body interprets as a signal to conserve energy. As a result, the basal metabolic rate decreases in order to prevent further weight gain, so there is a negative relationship between BMI and basal metabolic rate.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.011514660651051736, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7725368822875704, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.0008507952860721071, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2984616807756394}

