81. Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE)-[NONE]->Physical Activity Level
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2358931950447312, 'session_id': 'db262481-1601-42ec-943b-d831094eb4cc', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5522626296423725, 'prob_std': 0.21445444010622658, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08597946634701271, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6392078/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energy_expenditure'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8472781394797033, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation correctly identifies the distinction between the source and target variables. It states that Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) does not cause Physical Activity Level to change, but rather, Physical Activity Level is a determinant of TDEE. This is logically sound because TDEE is calculated based on components including basal metabolic rate, thermic effect of food, and physical activity. It would not make sense for TDEE, a summary outcome, to causally influence one of its own determinants (physical activity level). The explanation also correctly states there is no direct causal mechanism by which increasing TDEE would lead to increased Physical Activity Level, reinforcing the directionality of causation. The reasoning is internally consistent and scientifically coherent."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6767095328114697, 'motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) does not cause Physical Activity Level to change. Instead, Physical Activity Level is a determinant of TDEE, not the other way around. There is no direct causal mechanism by which increasing TDEE leads to increased Physical Activity Level.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.00633308166379675, 'perplexity': 1.1925395929326836, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8899172894164933, 'min_prob': 0.07633334389019576, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7530434772885084, 'token_prob_slope':