   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2003703807060877, 'session_id': 'db262481-1601-42ec-943b-d831094eb4cc', 'judge_perplexity': 1.63901824876712, 'prob_std': 0.17977518089552053, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0967619699030463, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6392078/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK591031/', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-27246-z', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10445668/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8778580716658074, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation clearly states that BMI does not directly cause changes in TDEE, but rather that any association between the two is mediated by variables such as Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) and Physical Activity Level. The explanation further notes that these mediators are already represented elsewhere in the causal loop diagram (CLD). This reasoning is logically sound: a direct causal relationship is only warranted if changes in the source variable (BMI) lead to changes in the target variable (TDEE) independently, not exclusively through intermediary variables. Since the explanation correctly identifies the lack of a direct effect and attributes any observed relationship to known mediators, the causal logic is coherent and well-articulated.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6514674574836512, 'motivation': 'Body Mass Index (BMI) does not directly cause Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) to change. The causal pathway operates through mediating variables such as Basal Metabolic Rate and Physical Activity Level, which are already included in the CLD. Therefore, there is no direct causal relationship from BMI to TDEE.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.01950745088306235, 'perplexity': 1.1313727128832451, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9135120828521136, 'min_prob': 0.15871255039665874, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7298719899559258, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00146372467416053, 'prob_variance': 0.03231911566601713, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0241424461473967, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00016068290295699676, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3110658610375724, 'avg_nll': 0.12343168562586151}

98. Body Mass Index (BMI)-[NEGATIVE]->Group-level BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2953826871084204, 'original_motivation': "Body Mass Index (BMI) causes Group-level BMI in a direct causal relationship. Group-level BMI is typically calculated as the aggregate (e.g., mean or median) of individual BMIs within a group. Therefore, an increase in an individual's BMI will directly increase the Group-level BMI, while a decrease will lower it.", 'session_id': 'db262481-1601-42ec-943b-d831094eb4cc', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7398553641664924, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0978269521265541, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Let\'s break down the explanation step by step:"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.627534790544669, 'motivation': "An individual's Body Mass Index (BMI) is inversely related to group-level BMI because when one person's BMI increases, it causes the average BMI of the group to decrease to maintain overall balance. This is due to a compensatory mechanism where higher individual BMIs are offset by lower BMIs in the rest of the group.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "An individual's Body Mass Index (BMI) is inversely related to group-level BMI because when one person's BMI increases, it causes the average BMI of the group to decrease to maintain overall balance. This is due to a compensatory mechanism where higher individual BMIs are offset by lower BMIs in the rest of the group.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.010229857100199032, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6994829897748354, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0003615466183228157, 'judge_prob_std': 0.31277300415245896}

